// What the title screen offers.
//
// A scenario is a world plus the units standing on it. Add one here and it appears on
// the menu — no Rust, no restart beyond the one you were going to do anyway.
//
// Order is the order they are listed, so it is your decision rather than an accident.
//
// FIELDS
//
//   name    what the button says
//   blurb   one line underneath, saying what is interesting about this one
//   world   the map file, as a path under `assets/`
//   units   where the pieces start
//
// The `world` path is NOT checked by the compiler — nothing here knows what a map is,
// deliberately, so that this file does not have to be edited whenever the map format
// changes. A typo is caught by a test that opens every world named here, so a wrong
// path fails `cargo test` rather than at the loading screen.
//
// COORDINATES are CUBE coordinates and MUST SUM TO ZERO: x + y + z == 0. That is what
// makes them a hex grid rather than three loose numbers.
// See https://www.redblobgames.com/grids/hexagons/
//
// A coordinate that does not sum to zero, or that has no ground a unit can stand on --
// off the edge of the map, or a spot with too little headroom -- is reported in the log
// and the unit falls back to the centre of the map. It does not stop the game, so a
// piece standing somewhere surprising is worth checking the terminal for.
(
    scenarios: [
        (
            name: "The Crossing",
            blurb: "A river with one bridge over it, a mountain, and a switchback up the side.",
            world: "config/world.ron",
            units: (
                // The centre of the map, which on this world is the bridge deck --
                // the river runs underneath.
                player: (x: 0, y: 0, z: 0),

                // Six hexes east: far enough to walk around before anything happens,
                // close enough to find without hunting.
                enemy: (x: 6, y: -6, z: 0),
            ),
        ),
        (
            name: "Rolling Hills",
            blurb: "Open procedural ground. Nowhere to funnel through, so distance is the only obstacle.",
            world: "config/worlds/rolling-hills.ron",
            units: (
                player: (x: 0, y: 0, z: 0),

                // Closer than on the Crossing, because there is no terrain in the way
                // to make the walk interesting.
                enemy: (x: 5, y: -5, z: 0),
            ),
        ),
    ],
)
